<http://data.silknow.org/event/ed5cb441-0c87-3d38-a64c-fc78b207453c>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "The tapestry was stated at time of purchase to have come from the Palazzo Giovio, Como . It was lent to the Museum by the Countess Lambertenghi in 1891 (see catalogue p.65). RP for loan : 1891/3988.\n\nHistorical significance: The tapestry is the finest example of its kind.\nThe borders of the tapestry are Italianate, with acanthus scrolls and grotesques with putti and masks and arms in the uprights."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/92b10fcf-88bd-3801-9c5a-9db3ce22cebb> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "The tapestry was stated at time of purchase to have come from the Palazzo Giovio, Como . It was lent to the Museum by the Countess Lambertenghi in 1891 (see catalogue p.65). RP for loan : 1891/3988.\n\nHistorical significance: The tapestry is the finest example of its kind.\nThe borders of the tapestry are Italianate, with acanthus scrolls and grotesques with putti and masks and arms in the uprights."@en .

